  "mechanisms": [
    "Light-induced non-image forming (NIF) system activation, which elicits greater endocrine, physiological, neurophysiological, and behavioral responses to shorter light wavelengths.",
    "Modulation of subcortical structures involved in alertness (e.g., thalamus/pulvinar) by light, which in turn dynamically promotes cortical activity in networks involved in ongoing nonvisual cognitive processes (e.g., attention networks).",
    "Dissipation of light effects over time, with region-specific time courses, similar to the transient enhancement of alertness."
  ],
  "moderators": [
    "Time of day (daytime vs. nighttime)",
