  "limitations": [
    "The study could not determine the relative contribution of different photoreceptors (classical visual vs. melanopsin) to the brain-response modulation, as the white-light source covered the whole visible spectrum.",
    "The study did not assess cognitive performance (e.g., reaction times) in normally rested subjects, only subjective alertness, which might differ from previous studies with sleep-deprived subjects.",
    "The statistical power of between-session contrasts at the random-effects level was limited for some regions, potentially leading to non-significant findings where effects might exist."
